# OS
.DS_Store

# Conversation summaries (generated at runtime) — plus dev-team's own
# .claude/memory/ bookkeeping relocated here by the #1406 .claude/-scoped
# artifact migration: /build's phase-state (build-phase.json — agent-
# instruction-written, no Python writer of its own) and /test-improve's
# per-slug resume state (test-improve/ — migrated via
# scripts/test_improve_resume.py's migrate_dir(); the sibling bare
# memory/test-improve/ rule below has been removed — this is its new home).
# decisions.md is untouched by any of these three rules — tracked by the
# absence of a matching rule, the same deny-by-default mechanism as the
# legacy memory/ block below (not a `!`-exception).
.claude/memory/*.md
.claude/memory/build-phase.json
.claude/memory/test-improve/
.claude/memory/archive/
.claude/memory/recon-*
# /repo-review's own per-run drift state (#1735) — regeneratable, and
# un-ignored would make it committable, which combined with an unvalidated
# read would be a hostile-PR delivery vector (see repo-review/SKILL.md § 2).
.claude/memory/repo-review-state.json

# Performance logs (generated at runtime)
.claude/metrics/*.json
.claude/metrics/*.log

# EnterWorktree tool scratch dirs (per-agent git worktrees, not repo content)
.claude/worktrees/
.claude/review-context/

# Per-session turn-state tracked by the code-intelligence nudge hooks — never repo content
.claude/code-intelligence-turn-state.json
.claude/code-intelligence-turn-state.json.lock

# Per-repo freeze scope-lock state read by pre_tool_guard.py (#1890) — transient
# runtime state, never repo content; un-ignored would make it committable, and
# it's read unvalidated by a guard whose allowed_patterns gate Write/Edit.
.claude/hooks/freeze-state.json

# Per-repo careful-mode state read by destructive_guard.py (#1900) — same
# transient-runtime-state class as freeze-state.json above; newly committable
# now that #1900 fixed its write path, so this rule is what keeps it from
# landing in git the moment a real `/careful` run writes it.
.claude/hooks/careful-state.json

# /setup and /project-init's stack-detection cache — pure detection output, the
# same regeneratable-artifact class as .claude/memory/ and .claude/metrics/
# above. /setup's Step 11 downstream-only ignore-rule step is explicitly
# skipped when running in-repo (this repo curates its own .gitignore instead),
# so this rule is what keeps a `/setup` run here from leaving it untracked and
# capture-prone (issue #1487).
.claude/project-stack.json

# /project-init's Step 4c code-lookup decision state (which of CodeGraph /
# Repowise / Graphify were installed, declined, or built --code-only). Same
# machine-local, regeneratable, capture-prone class as the stack cache above
# and written by the same /setup -> /project-init pass, so it needs the same
# rule — the in-repo skip of /setup's Step 11 leaves it untracked otherwise.
.claude/init-state.json

# Runtime metrics — ignored by default (deny-by-default: metrics/ is
# generated-runtime-data territory — session digests, telemetry, review-value,
# verify-log, boundary-events, cost-metering, learning-loop state, ... — a new
# metrics file should need an explicit un-ignore to land in git, not the other
# way around). Resolution is now git-root-based (artifact_paths.py, #1406),
# not cwd-dependent, so every runtime metrics file lands under a single
# `.claude/metrics/` at the project root — the leading **/ is belt-and-braces
# (covers any stray non-`.claude`-nested metrics/ tree, e.g. a legacy
# not-yet-migrated file) rather than load-bearing the way it was under #1081's
# cwd-dependent resolution.
**/metrics/*
# …but keep the deliberately-tracked audit trails.
!**/metrics/config-changelog.jsonl
!**/metrics/eval-variance.jsonl
# gate-bypass-audit.jsonl (#1831 follow-up, #1945 Slice 1): pre_pr_review.py's
# existing dispatch-ledger corroboration (review_gate_corroboration.py,
# >=2-distinct-agent evaluation) already satisfies "a delegated subagent can
# be PR-gated without a bypass, without self-writing the gate file" — this
# rule only makes the resulting audit record durable past worktree removal;
# it does not reintroduce commit-time gating (pre_commit_review.py stays a
# documented no-op per #1886).
!**/metrics/gate-bypass-audit.jsonl
# verify-log.jsonl is deliberately exempt from the .claude/-nested migration
# (AC3) and stays permanently at the bare top-level metrics/verify-log.jsonl —
# already denied by the **/metrics/* catch-all above; this explicit line
# guards against that catch-all being narrowed or removed later under the
# mistaken assumption that all metrics/ content has fully relocated.
metrics/verify-log.jsonl

# Effort-band model routing (per-user, never checked in)
# - ladder: optional ordered model list (.claude/model-ladder.json), hand-written by users behind restricted endpoints
# - session model: captured at SessionStart for dispatch fallback + upgrade flags
# - bump log: append-only JSONL recording routing bumps from the dispatch hook
.claude/model-ladder.json
.claude/session-model
.claude/metrics/model-routing.log
UPDATE.md

sync-to-aci.sh

